# CLAUDE.md

This file provides guidance to Claude Code (claude.ai/code) when working with code in this repository.

## Commands

This project uses [uv](https://github.com/astral-sh/uv) for dependency and environment management.

```bash
# Install dependencies
uv sync

# Add a new dependency
uv add <package>

# Run a script
uv run test.py

# Run a specific Python file
uv run python -m pytest  # if tests are added later
```

The package is installed in editable mode from `src/`, so changes to source files are reflected immediately without reinstalling.

## Environment Setup

Copy the required env vars into a `.env` file at the project root. `test.py` loads it via `python-dotenv`:

```
API_KEY=<your-openai-compatible-api-key>
BASE_URL=<api-base-url>       # defaults to localhost:11434
MODEL_NAME=<model-name>       # defaults to gpt-oss:120b-cloud
```

## Architecture

The library extracts knowledge graphs from text using LLMs. The pipeline is:

```
Document → Prompt (schema-driven) → LLM → JSON repair → Parse/clean → Format → Filter → GraphDocument
```

**Source layout:** `src/LLMGraphTransformer/`

### Layer breakdown

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `schema.py` | Data models — `NodeSchema`, `RelationshipSchema` (plain classes for user input); `Node`, `Relationship`, `GraphDocument` (Pydantic, for output) |
| `prompt_generation.py` | Builds a `ChatPromptTemplate` from the user's schemas, encoding allowed node types, relationships, properties, and any `additional_instructions` |
| `main.py` | Orchestrates the full pipeline: LLM invocation, JSON repair via `json_repair`, property cleanup, ID/type formatting, and strict-mode filtering |
| `__init__.py` | Re-exports `LLMGraphTransformer` from `main.py` |

### Key behaviors in `main.py`

- **`process_properties(props)`**: Sanitizes LLM output — drops empty lists, unwraps single-element lists to scalars, logs a warning if `props` is not a dict.
- **`_parse_and_clean_json(parsed_json)`**: Builds `Node` and `Relationship` objects from raw JSON; uses a `node_map` keyed by node ID to resolve relationship endpoints.
- **`_format_graph()`**: Normalizes output — node IDs and types are title-cased, relationship types are uppercased with spaces converted to underscores.
- **`graph_strict_mode_filtering()`**: Post-LLM filter that drops nodes/relationships not matching the declared schemas (case-insensitive). Active when `strict_mode=True` (the default).
- **`convert_to_graph_document(document)`**: Single-document entry point. `convert_to_graph_documents(documents)` is the batch wrapper.

### Schema-driven prompting

`prompt_generation.py` dynamically renders the allowed schemas into the system prompt so the LLM knows exactly which node types, relationship types, and properties are valid. Passing `additional_instructions` appends extra rules verbatim to the prompt.

### LLM compatibility

The library is LangChain-native and accepts any `BaseLanguageModel`. The canonical integration is `ChatOpenAI` pointed at an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, but any chat model that can return JSON works.
